00:40:12,062 --> 00:40:12,862
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, less real.

579
00:40:13,102 --> 00:40:15,463
[SPEAKER_02]: I think that that really sums it up for most people.

580
00:40:16,304 --> 00:40:21,205
[SPEAKER_02]: I think that's exactly the main, the core of the Kutujana's problem and lack, to be honest, of nāmasikāra.

581
00:40:22,486 --> 00:40:26,187
[SPEAKER_02]: They don't recognize that things that are less real are real as such.

582
00:40:28,468 --> 00:40:34,770
[SPEAKER_02]: So, they keep maintaining the threshold, the measure of what feels real for them, what feels really real.

583
00:40:35,431 --> 00:40:41,213
[SPEAKER_02]: They measure things against that, you know, failing to understand that, well, something less real is still real as such.

584
00:40:42,952 --> 00:40:45,553
[SPEAKER_03]: You find it difficult.

585
00:40:46,313 --> 00:40:48,314
[SPEAKER_03]: It kind of indicates that it's real.

586
00:40:48,994 --> 00:40:50,774
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, exactly.

587
00:40:50,994 --> 00:40:52,535
[SPEAKER_03]: How could you talk about it?

588
00:40:53,035 --> 00:40:55,476
[SPEAKER_03]: It would not be manifested in which this is not real.

589
00:40:57,916 --> 00:41:00,277
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it's a repeated recognition of that.

590
00:41:00,877 --> 00:41:03,218
[SPEAKER_02]: If less real things are real as such.

591
00:41:06,078 --> 00:41:09,139
[SPEAKER_02]: Not real as much, but real as such.

592
00:41:09,279 --> 00:41:09,639
[SPEAKER_02]: As such.

593
00:41:09,939 --> 00:41:10,280
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

594
00:41:12,512 --> 00:41:23,067
[SPEAKER_00]: But the standard you use for determining what is real, I guess that is why central strength comes to make that standard.

595
00:41:24,139 --> 00:41:28,301
